# SymbiYosys job for eog_regs (Verify role, task T1.regs.fv). Properties: fv_eog_regs.sv (G1-G7, R_*, covers).
#   bash scripts/formal.sh regs          # all tasks, report in reports/formal_regs.txt
#
# Harness parameters: N_FAC = 2, RES_DEPTH = 2, AL_DEPTH = 2, N_WELL = 8, CYC_PER_MS = 4 (see the harness header).
# eog_regs has no multiplier, so there is no abstract/real split; every task sees the same design.
#
# prove_* : PDR (abc pdr), unbounded, one task per property group (the other assertions are removed with chformal so
#           each PDR run sees a small cone; one combined run did not converge in 50 min). Prove tasks read the harness
#           with -DFV_QUIET: tap/stall/DBG/al_drop/ms_since_hb inputs held quiet (they feed only STATS/DBG, which the
#           testbench checks) and STATS 0 / 12 counted to 15 (equal 32-bit counters are hard for PDR).
#           k-induction is not used: the DUT's AXI pipeline, sweep counter, FIFO pointers and DATA beat counter are
#           invisible at the ports, so port-level properties are not inductive without internal invariants (the
#           independence rule keeps the RTL's internals out of the harness).
#   prove_axi  G1_*, u_d.ax_*            prove_ctl  R_ctrl R_led R_dsel R_id R_unm R_status
#   prove_rd   R_rw G7_rd R_wb            prove_puls G4_* G7_* (not G7_rd) R_wbw*
#   prove_cfg  G2 G2_port G2_port_c       prove_cq<k> G2_row_q<k> G2_rd_q<k> (CONFIG words 4k..4k+3)
#   prove_glb  G3*
#   prove_fifo G5_*                       prove_data G6_* R_rec
# bmc   : abc bmc3 (smtbmc/boolector took > 10 min to reach step 10 on this design), every assertion from reset,
#         depth 14 (reset + sweep + 2-3 AXI transactions, or a push and its first beats). Quick counterexamples
#         only: every assertion is proven unbounded by the prove_* tasks; steps beyond ~15 cost several minutes each.
# cover : the spec's cover (CONFIG row written, slot enabled, DATA record pushed, RESULT read back) and sanity
#         covers; depth 40.
#
# Run times against the verifier's throwaway stub (never committed), all tasks in parallel (sby default) on the shared
# WSL machine, Sun Nov 8 ~04:30 CST: all PASS. prove_puls 38 s, prove_axi 44 s, prove_ctl 76 s, prove_cfg 77 s,
# prove_rd 88 s, prove_glb 343 s, prove_cq0..3 432-546 s, prove_fifo 946 s, prove_data 958 s, cover 42 s (C_main at
# step 22), bmc 110 s. Wall clock ~16 min. A timeout of 1800 s per prove task leaves ~2x margin.

[tasks]
prove_axi prove
prove_ctl prove
prove_rd prove
prove_puls prove
prove_cfg prove
prove_cq0 prove
prove_cq1 prove
prove_cq2 prove
prove_cq3 prove
prove_glb prove
prove_fifo prove
prove_data prove
bmc
cover

[options]
prove: mode prove
prove: timeout 1800
bmc:   mode bmc
bmc:   depth 14
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 40

[engines]
prove: abc pdr
bmc:   abc bmc3
cover: smtbmc boolector

[script]
read_verilog -formal -sv eog_fv_props.sv
read_verilog -formal -sv -I . eog_regs.sv
prove: read_verilog -formal -sv -I . -DFV_QUIET fv_eog_regs.sv
~prove: read_verilog -formal -sv -I . fv_eog_regs.sv
prep -top fv_eog_regs
memory -nomap
memory_map
# out-of-range dynamic selects (e.g. a 5-bit slot index into an N_FAC = 2 table) become x after techmap; the
# AIG engines reject x, so map first and make every remaining x a free value
flatten
techmap
opt -fast
setundef -undriven -anyseq
setundef -anyseq
# prove_*: keep only that group's assertions (one PDR run per group keeps the cones small)
prove_axi: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G1_* c:*ax_* %u %d
prove_ctl: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:R_ctrl c:R_led c:R_dsel c:R_id c:R_unm c:R_status %u %u %u %u %u %d
prove_rd: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:R_rw c:G7_rd c:R_wb %u %u %d
prove_puls: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G4_* c:G7_* c:R_wbw* %u %u c:G7_rd %d %d
prove_cfg: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G2 c:G2_port %u c:G2_port_c %u %d
prove_cq0: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G2_row_q0 c:G2_rd_q0 %u %d
prove_cq1: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G2_row_q1 c:G2_rd_q1 %u %d
prove_cq2: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G2_row_q2 c:G2_rd_q2 %u %d
prove_cq3: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G2_row_q3 c:G2_rd_q3 %u %d
prove_glb: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G3* %d
prove_fifo: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G5_* %d
prove_data: chformal -assert -remove c:* c:G6_* c:R_rec %u %d

[files]
../common/eog_fv_props.sv
../../rtl/eog_defs.svh
../../rtl/eog_regs.sv
fv_eog_regs.sv
